            "notes": "### Powers:\nIf you're struggling to get in or you are not at all struggling to get in, [Dragon's Breath](item_32dc8374-7541-46fb-9891-29b7fbe9ed4d) can give you poke and massive aoe damage to get ahead.\nOtherwise if you can get close enough for the blade to connect, the 60% lifesteal on blade is healing and during blade you're near immortal (of course results may vary but [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) op).\n\n---\n### Items:\nThis round, depending on the money either gives you huge power or huge survivability. There's not much survivability in the purple items that you want (besides [Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643)), but since it's hybrid you can grab any of the lifesteal items like [Energized Bracers](item_f83a1d9e-91f8-4d2c-bd62-c673b8d9fd2e), [Technoleech](item_cb7fd8bf-bdcc-439a-ad35-372f24a027a8), or [Skyline Nanites](item_0b334927-da04-42d6-8dfd-96e7b6c1cd51) if you're against Pharah/Mercy. If you don't care about survivability, [Custom Stock](item_17d633af-8bcc-4893-b865-be0a7bc66fe2) is a great buy along with [Wrist Wraps](item_19183386-c859-42ca-93f2-355d47d01e36), [Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054), or [Nano Cola](item_79b22609-8046-4a8a-a5a2-bb49cd7e11c6).",
